  "note": "0.4.328: the owner asked for more variety in the cast's facial hair (\"many of them share that little chin strip\"). The painter's three bearded styles all drew one thin line round the jaw; it now draws thirteen (stubble, shadow, patchy, goatee, short, full, chops, walrus, pencil, handlebar, horseshoe, chinstrap and the original moustache), and the bearded looks are spread across them. Only the beard pixels on the front, sides and underside of the head change; every sheet keeps its size and opacity. The Drisking sheets are unchanged.",
